{"i":3,"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"path\": \"nl0/templates/quantified-implication-example.md\", \"total_lines\": 164, \"start\": 1, \"end\": 164, \"start_column\": 0, \"end_column\": 78, \"requested_end\": 220, \"has_more\": false, \"next_start\": null, \"next_column\": 0, \"next_end\": null, \"text\": \"1: # Neutral quantified implication example\\n2: \\n3: This is a complete format example, not a test solution or an Audit A receipt.\\n4: The target has no original hypotheses. The antecedent r=0 belongs under a new\\n5: universal binder, so it is a temporary L1 inside R001, not a new H root and not\\n6: a property granted by the ambient type of r. F001 remains under L1; F002 is\\n7: the complete implication after discharge. Neither an unconditional r*r=0 nor\\n8: a conclusion about one unspecified r can replace the quantified target.\\n9: \\n10: ```json\\n11: {\\n12:   \\\"spec\\\": {\\n13:     \\\"format_version\\\": 2,\\n14:     \\\"case_id\\\": \\\"neutral-quantified-implication\\\",\\n15:     \\\"full_target\\\": \\\"For every real number r, r=0 implies r*r=0.\\\",\\n16:     \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"For every real number r, r=0 implies r*r=0.\\\",\\n17:     \\\"parameters\\\": [],\\n18:     \\\"hypotheses\\\": [],\\n19:     \\\"definitions\\\": [],\\n20:     \\\"logic\\\": {\\n21:       \\\"classical\\\": false,\\n22:       \\\"rules\\\": [\\n23:         \\\"direct\\\",\\n24:         \\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\n25:         \\\"forall_introduction\\\"\\n26:       ]\\n27:     },\\n28:     \\\"pins\\\": {\\n29:       \\\"lean_version\\\": \\\"controller-bound\\\",\\n30:       \\\"mathlib_commit\\\": \\\"controller-bound\\\",\\n31:       \\\"mathlib_root\\\": \\\"controller-bound\\\"\\n32:     },\\n33:     \\\"inputs\\\": []\\n34:   },\\n35:   \\\"graph\\\": {\\n36:     \\\"format_version\\\": 2,\\n37:     \\\"case_id\\\": \\\"neutral-quantified-implication\\\",\\n38:     \\\"spec_sha256\\\": \\\"controller-bound\\\",\\n39:     \\\"propositions\\\": [\\n40:       {\\n41:         \\\"id\\\": \\\"P\\\",\\n42:         \\\"kind\\\": \\\"target\\\",\\n43:         \\\"statement\\\": \\\"For every real number r, r=0 implies r*r=0.\\\",\\n44:         \\\"definitions\\\": [],\\n45:         \\\"binders\\\": [\\n46:           {\\n47:             \\\"symbol\\\": \\\"r\\\",\\n48:             \\\"type\\\": \\\"real number\\\"\\n49:           }\\n50:         ],\\n51:         \\\"objects\\\": [\\n52:           \\\"r\\\",\\n53:           \\\"0\\\"\\n54:         ]\\n55:       }\\n56:     ],\\n57:     \\\"inferences\\\": [\\n58:       {\\n59:         \\\"id\\\": \\\"R001\\\",\\n60:         \\\"inputs\\\": [],\\n61:         \\\"output\\\": \\\"P\\\",\\n62:         \\\"definitions\\\": [],\\n63:         \\\"rules\\\": [\\n64:           \\\"direct\\\",\\n65:           \\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\n66:           \\\"forall_introduction\\\"\\n67:         ],\\n68:         \\\"locals\\\": [\\n69:           {\\n70:             \\\"symbol\\\": \\\"r\\\",\\n71:             \\\"type\\\": \\\"real number\\\",\\n72:             \\\"scope\\\": \\\"R001/argument\\\",\\n73:             \\\"start\\\": \\\"S001\\\",\\n74:             \\\"end\\\": \\\"S003\\\",\\n75:             \\\"kind\\\": \\\"arbitrary\\\",\\n76:             \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Fix an arbitrary real number r.\\\",\\n77:             \\\"from_inputs\\\": [],\\n78:             \\\"from_local\\\": [],\\n79:             \\\"objects\\\": []\\n80:           }\\n81:         ],\\n82:         \\\"argument\\\": [\\n83:           {\\n84:             \\\"id\\\": \\\"S001\\\",\\n85:             \\\"text\\\": \\\"Fix an arbitrary real number r. Temporarily assume L1: r=0. Record F001: r=0.\\\",\\n86:             \\\"uses\\\": [],\\n87:             \\\"uses_local\\\": [],\\n88:             \\\"objects\\\": [\\n89:               \\\"r\\\",\\n90:               \\\"0\\\"\\n91:             ],\\n92:             \\\"produces\\\": [\\n93:               {\\n94:                 \\\"id\\\": \\\"F001\\\",\\n95:                 \\\"statement\\\": \\\"r=0.\\\",\\n96:                 \\\"binders\\\": [],\\n97:                 \\\"objects\\\": [\\n98:                   \\\"r\\\",\\n99:                   \\\"0\\\"\\n100:                 ],\\n101:                 \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n102:                   \\\"L1\\\"\\n103:                 ]\\n104:               }\\n105:             ],\\n106:             \\\"introduces\\\": [\\n107:               \\\"L1\\\"\\n108:             ],\\n109:             \\\"discharges\\\": []\\n110:           },\\n111:           {\\n112:             \\\"id\\\": \\\"S002\\\",\\n113:             \\\"text\\\": \\\"Under L1, F001 gives r=0. Substitution in r*r gives 0*0=0 by the zero law. Discharge L1 by implication introduction: if r=0 then r*r=0. This full implication is F002.\\\",\\n114:             \\\"uses\\\": [],\\n115:             \\\"uses_local\\\": [\\n116:               \\\"F001\\\"\\n117:             ],\\n118:             \\\"objects\\\": [\\n119:               \\\"r\\\",\\n120:               \\\"0\\\"\\n121:             ],\\n122:             \\\"produces\\\": [\\n123:               {\\n124:                 \\\"id\\\": \\\"F002\\\",\\n125:                 \\\"statement\\\": \\\"If r=0 then r*r=0.\\\",\\n126:                 \\\"binders\\\": [],\\n127:                 \\\"objects\\\": [\\n128:                   \\\"r\\\",\\n129:                   \\\"0\\\"\\n130:                 ],\\n131:                 \\\"assumptions\\\": []\\n132:               }\\n133:             ],\\n134:             \\\"introduces\\\": [],\\n135:             \\\"discharges\\\": [\\n136:               \\\"L1\\\"\\n137:             ]\\n138:           },\\n139:           {\\n140:             \\\"id\\\": \\\"S003\\\",\\n141:             \\\"text\\\": \\\"F002 holds for the arbitrary r, and no local assumption remains. Universal introduction therefore proves: for every real number r, r=0 implies r*r=0.\\\",\\n142:             \\\"uses\\\": [],\\n143:             \\\"uses_local\\\": [\\n144:               \\\"F002\\\"\\n145:             ],\\n146:             \\\"objects\\\": [\\n147:               \\\"r\\\",\\n148:               \\\"0\\\"\\n149:             ],\\n150:             \\\"produces\\\": [],\\n151:             \\\"introduces\\\": [],\\n152:             \\\"discharges\\\": []\\n153:           }\\n154:         ],\\n155:         \\\"applications\\\": []\\n156:       }\\n157:     ]\\n158:   }\\n159: }\\n160: ```\\n161: \\n162: The fixed finite algebra justifies the zero law; no analysis/linear-algebra theorem\\n163: is granted. This demonstrates binder/assumption accounting only. Independent\\n164: Audit A still checks the actual mathematics, declarations and complete output.\"}"}
{"i":4,"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"path\": \"nl0/references/audit-a.md\", \"total_lines\": 143, \"start\": 1, \"end\": 143, \"start_column\": 0, \"end_column\": 78, \"requested_end\": 180, \"has_more\": false, \"next_start\": null, \"next_column\": 0, \"next_end\": null, \"text\": \"1: # Audit A: mathematical review in Yui\\n2: \\n3: <!-- yui-nl0-acceptance:begin -->\\n4: ## Shared mathematical acceptance requirements\\n5: \\n6: Contract version: `yui-nl0-audit-a-2`.\\n7: \\n8: The author and independent auditor use this same mathematical standard. NL0\\n9: reviews a complete natural-language proof and necessary mathematical detail.\\n10: Specific Lean declarations, signatures, representations and proof tactics are\\n11: implementation work for nl02lean, not prerequisites for ordinary NL0 review.\\n12: The following grouped criteria replace V1's ten separate per-R report rows.\\n13: \\n14: | ID | Review group | Author evidence group | Requirement |\\n15: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n16: | `target` | package | original_context_note | Preserve the complete original theorem, every original H, quantifier, domain, normalization and supplied core proof route. A parameter or definition cannot hide a hypothesis or desired conclusion. |\\n17: | `definitions` | package | declaration_check | Define mathematical objects and notation sufficiently for their actual uses. Check types, dependencies, construction guards and legitimate local introductions. A definition grants no unproved property. |\\n18: | `sources` | package | original_context_note | Check complete E statements, primary-source identity, context and conditions under the source policy. An explicitly selected native M retains its bound signature checks; authors need not introduce M nodes for ordinary mathematical background. Unavailable originals remain disclosed UNVERIFIED source assumptions. |\\n19: | `structure` | package | original_context_note | Verify the actual AND dependency graph, unique producers, absence of cycles and faithful exported statements. Retain every original H and disclose unused H. Internal results are proved, never new roots. |\\n20: | `statement_closure` | closure | output_notes | Inputs and output state the mathematical content, objects, domains, quantifiers and conditions their consumers need. Check actual object occurrences and definitions. No missing identification can be supplied by an absent producer proof or a paper equation number. |\\n21: | `dependency_closure` | closure | dependency_and_local_assumption_check | Check direct input use, earlier local facts, witness existence and proper discharge of assumptions. No circular dependency, future fact or escaped local object is allowed. Mathematically checked routine background may supplement the packet without prior native lookup. |\\n22: | `argument` | inference | dependency_and_local_assumption_check | Verify the complete implication and every output clause at ordinary rigorous mathematical granularity, including material limiting operations, domains and regularity. Compress correct routine reasoning; locate a real gap rather than requiring a transcript of elementary steps. |\\n23: | `applicability` | inference | source_application_check | Check actual instantiations and all material premises of invoked E/M or routine background facts, with grounds in inputs or earlier local derivations. Required bridges are proved. A familiar theorem name or a proposed Lean tactic supplies no mathematical justification. |\\n24: \\n25: ### Scope and mathematical boundary\\n26: \\n27: Global review owns target/H fidelity, definitions, source statements and graph\\n28: consistency. Each local reviewer owns the conditional implication at its R\\n29: node. Conditional packet replay has a different input boundary: these statements are conditional premises.\\n30: The local reviewer does not re-prove an input N or re-audit its source paper;\\n31: the graph and that producer's review establish those separate obligations.\\n32: Conversely, an input N exports only its full statement, not unexported facts\\n33: from the producer's body. The fifth local criterion, packet_replay, assesses\\n34: sufficiency under this exact boundary. The controller records execution\\n35: identity and exposure independently of the mathematical judgment.\\n36: \\n37: Review correctness rather than the number of displayed lines. Ordinary valid\\n38: textbook compression is allowed. Material missing hypotheses, witnesses,\\n39: constructions, scope discharges or core arguments are not implementation gaps.\\n40: Return them for located author repair and fresh review. No theorem needs to be re-proved\\n41: when its legitimate mathematical source and actual application suffice.\\n42: \\n43: The domain-neutral elementary-language-4 profile retains equality, supplied\\n44: definitions, finite arithmetic/order reasoning and finite sums. It is syntax\\n45: and elementary calculation policy, not a subject vocabulary or theorem list.\\n46: Objects from any field use problem parameters, D definitions or scoped locals.\\n47: Neither an author-written calculation list nor a familiar symbol adds a theorem.\\n48: \\n49: ### Mathematical background: mathematical-background-v2-1\\n50: \\n51: A reviewer may positively assess a routine, local mathematical fact without\\n52: first finding its Mathlib declaration. Record its precise mathematical\\n53: statement, actual argument location, available condition grounds and a short\\n54: mathematical justification in a background note. Use kind mathematical for an\\n55: ordinary background result and elementary for a useful elementary completion.\\n56: This is an actual mathematical judgment, not a future TODO or a claim of\\n57: native verification. Do not record every algebraic operation.\\n58: \\n59: Eligibility requires a correct standard local step with all premises already\\n60: available, no new H and no substantial new core proof or changed route.\\n61: Important external tools remain explicit E inputs; a missing project result\\n62: or uncertain source cannot be waived as background. If an explicitly supplied\\n63: native mathlib note is retained, its full bound evidence is still validated.\\n64: No field-specific whitelist determines eligibility.\\n65: \\n66: The accepted authority is immutable author NL0 plus its hash-bound mathematical\\n67: review supplement. It is a natural-language audit under the mathematical-background policy, not a\\n68: detailed-NL0 format-3 native-background receipt. At nl02lean, workers must discharge all necessary\\n69: facts by actual Lean proofs or checked library use; a note never becomes an\\n70: unproved H, axiom or extra external assumption. The exact implementation may\\n71: differ while preserving the mathematical meaning.\\n72: \\n73: ### Actual review and result qualification\\n74: \\n75: Independent reviewers assess the actual content; schema validation does not\\n76: prove mathematics. An unexamined item remains unread/read. A mathematical\\n77: uncertainty is assessed UNVERIFIED, not PASS. Missing or conflicting assessments\\n78: block acceptance. Ordinary source-access deferral follows the conditional-source\\n79: policy and must appear in final warnings; it cannot yield unqualified PASS.\\n80: \\n81: Use short located reasons for straightforward PASS items and enough detail to\\n82: make a defect or uncertainty actionable. Avoid duplicate explanations across\\n83: criteria. A concise report still covers every required mathematical check.\\n84: Do not read author self-check notes, old verdicts, other R proof bodies, other\\n85: case results or personal proof skills to manufacture independent approval.\\n86: <!-- yui-nl0-acceptance:end -->\\n87: \\n88: ## Execution protocol\\n89: \\n90: 1. Freeze the original problem, spec and NL0. A separate fresh global reviewer\\n91:    reads the exhaustive global-overview.json, relevant canonical content and\\n92:    source evidence. Review each D and selected E/M; the overview is data, not\\n93:    an assessment. Do not infer absence from a partial page.\\n94: 2. Complete global source/graph review before dispatching local R reviews.\\n95:    Up to the explicitly confirmed N independent R reviewers work concurrently.\\n96:    Each receives only its own packet and mathematical-NL0 rules. Review full arguments,\\n97:    actual applications and definitions; input N statements are conditional.\\n98: 3. Prefer one complete artifact with an explicit coverage map. Use\\n99:    record_review_item and read_review_progress only for useful checkpoints.\\n100:    record_background_note is optional; a complete artifact may include its\\n101:    actual notes directly. Batch reading several declared fragments is available.\\n102: 4. Each local report has inference, packet_sha256, verdict, notes, checks,\\n103:    findings and optional background_notes. The checks map contains exactly\\n104:    statement_closure, dependency_closure, argument, applicability, packet_replay.\\n105:    Each row has verdict, notes and resolving packet locations. E applications\\n106:    additionally retain actual binding, per-hypothesis, conclusion and bridge\\n107:    assessments; this is mathematical applicability, not a Lean API inventory.\\n108: 5. Global reports have target_review, definition_reviews, source_reviews,\\n109:    structure_review and findings. Each E adds citation_checks for\\n110:    literature_identity, result_location, statement_fidelity,\\n111:    context_completeness, version_and_eligibility. Inaccessible primary text\\n112:    leaves blocked checks UNVERIFIED while remaining assessment continues.\\n113: 6. A blocking finding needs its actual location, explanation and a short exact\\n114:    quotation from that location. Preserve the defect and untouched coverage.\\n115:    Return located mathematical repairs to the author; review changed scopes\\n116:    independently. Do not resample a mathematical rejection or silently erase it.\\n117: 7. The collector checks complete coverage, consistency, exact bytes and actual\\n118:    independent execution before producing the audit-format-4 receipt.\\n119:    Old detailed-NL0 format-3 receipts are not silently upgraded. Inherited format-4 judgments retain\\n120:    their original source/rule hashes, exposure and costs.\\n121: \\n122: ## Sources, scopes and final handoff\\n123: \\n124: Use [external theorem review](external-theorems.md) and\\n125: [conditional sources](conditional-sources.md) for source identity, exact\\n126: statements and warnings. Reuse adequate original text; several theorem uses\\n127: may share one staged readback. Each application still discharges its own\\n128: premises. No successful download or guessed Mathlib availability is approval.\\n129: \\n130: Use [logical rules](logical-rules.md) for local scopes and\\n131: [background notes](background-notes.md) for the mathematical supplement.\\n132: The ordinary complete result remains relative to explicit E assumptions.\\n133: An inaccessible E original permits only a source-qualified result. Translation\\n134: retains this exact audit and supplement until reviewed mathematical changes\\n135: invalidate affected scopes. Typed interfaces, native checking, standalone\\n136: assembly and independent semantic Audit B are separate later gates.\\n137: \\n138: ## Paywalled or inaccessible primary text\\n139: \\n140: Follow [conditional sources](conditional-sources.md). Preserve the complete\\n141: secondary statement and actual access evidence; unavailable source checks\\n142: stay UNVERIFIED. Continue other work only with an explicitly qualified source\\n143: assumption, and report warn.json/warn.md. No unqualified full PASS is granted.\"}"}

