node("N001",`There is A=A(T,gamma,R)<infinity such that every real mean-zero initial datum f0 in H^gamma with ||f0||_(H^gamma)<=R has a unique exact KdV solution in the convention D012 and sup_[0,T]||u(t)||_(H^gamma)<=A. Smooth initial data give smooth solutions, with the same H^gamma bound. Thus the twisted v=S_(-t)u obeys M<=1+A uniformly on this ball. For any B>0, two real mean-zero initial L2 data with norm sum <=B have flows satisfying sup_[0,T]||u-tilde u||_2<=C(T,B)||u0-tilde u0||_2. In particular real mean-zero Fourier polynomial approximations to H^gamma data converge in C([0,T];L2) to this solution.`,["D001","D002","D003","D004","D005","D012"],[b("f0","periodic distribution"),b("u","time-dependent periodic distribution"),b("v","time-dependent periodic distribution"),b("A","real constant"),b("B","positive real")],["T","gamma","R","Ttor","Fourier","H","L2","S","KdV","f0","u","v","A","B"],"problem.md:105–122,632–634; source-sign and norm bridge.");
