s("S001",`Fix arbitrary smooth real mean-zero datum and integer L>=1. H001 gives tau=T/L>0. N005 ensures all iterates are smooth, real and mean-zero. In E005 set tau_s=tau, t_j=t_n and f=v^n=S_(-t_n)u^n. The source exponentials exp(t partial_x^3) are S_(-t), its quadratic stage is F_n, its A^n is C_n(t_(n+1)), and its R_2^n is exactly D014 with t0=t_n: both alpha=3ab(a+b), beta=3kc(a+b), phase and coefficient -tau/(18ik) agree. The source update (1.4) equals D009–D011 term by term, including its mean term tau/9 and final endpoint term -1/(27tau). Therefore E005 gives the displayed identity for v^(n+1).`,["H001","N005","E005"],[],["T","S","Psi","Remainder","Bop","Stage","Interp"],[f("F001","On each step v^(n+1)=f_n+F_n(end)+C_n(end)-Remainder_(t_n,tau)(f_n,f_n,f_n).",["Psi","Remainder","Stage","Interp"])]),
s("S002",`In D023 every stage and integral vanishes at t_n. At t_(n+1), Q_n cancels its part in W_n, so F001 gives exactly V(t_(n+1))=v^(n+1); V(t_n)=v^n. Thus adjoining step values agree. Differentiation on a step gives F_n'=(1/2)Bop_t(f_n,f_n), C_n'=Bop_t(f_n,F_n), Q_n'=(1/2)Bop_t(F_n,F_n), so Y_n'=Bop_t(f_n,F_n)+(1/2)Bop_t(F_n,F_n)-W_n/tau and V'=(1/2)Bop_t(z_n,z_n)-W_n/tau. From the definition of Rres and V=z_n+Y_n, subtracting the two cross and square terms yields V'=(1/2)Bop_t(V,V)+Rres'. Each rho_n starts at zero, so Rres concatenates continuously. Every Bop output and Remainder output has zero mean, as do the initial states; hence all claimed mean restrictions hold. Continuity across the finite grid makes the piecewise differential identity global in distributions, with no jumps.`,[],["F001"],["S","Psi","Remainder","Bop","Stage","Interp"])
